Please excuse the lack of included context but I think it's fair to say
that the current test-framework and scripts are at the end of their
evolutionary life and that whilst they will be required to fulfil a role in
test for the foreseeable future what is required is a vastly more capable
and scalable approach to testing Lustre in particular and massively
parallel exascale file systems in general.

